  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed value near $13.11B (+1.8% 30D) leaves tokenized-cash balances largely range-bound\u2014the market story this week is more about issuer and distribution news than a shift in AUM. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-08-18-securitize-neubergers-230-billion-fixed-income-platform-onchain-new-tokenized-fund-412102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize brings Neuberger\u2019s $230 billion fixed-income platform onchain with new tokenized fund</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~41% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~39% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~6% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/neuberger-launches-tokenized-fixed-income-fund-with-securitize?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Neuberger teams with Securitize on multi-chain tokenized fixed-income fund launch</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Settlement economics are reshaping network share:</strong> Fee and throughput advantages can pull 30D network-share toward the chains that keep settlement cheaper and more operationally reliable. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/18/visa-is-looking-for-a-new-stablecoin-settlement-partner-now-that-bvnk-is-owned-by-mastercard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Visa looking for new stablecoin settlement partner after BVNK sale to Mastercard</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. USYC, BUIDL, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/18/hashkey-taps-hong-kong-s-first-regulated-stablecoin-to-settle-insurance-and-trade-deals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">HashKey taps Hong Kong&#x27;s first regulated stablecoin to settle insurance and trade deals</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
